{
  "stage": "write",
  "item": "ch06.s01",
  "inputs_hash": "c3d6873b14208c09bdda9d7c2d7312a8517962c45a6a07738e8a6361d5b2b026",
  "output_hash": "9009aae56405077448de6ef26c0e38755ebf3df126edb559cd0f6738c3462dd2",
  "output": {
    "section_id": "ch06.s01",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "ch06.s01.p01",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p01.01",
            "text": "Why is instruction fine-tuning needed when a model is already pre-trained?",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p01.02",
            "text": "Pre-trained LLMs are good at text completion, but they struggle with following specific instructions.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@32",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@34",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@36"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p01.03",
            "text": "Examples of such instructions include fixing the grammar in a text and converting a text into passive voice.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@39",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@41",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@43"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p01.04",
            "text": "Because a pre-trained LLM does not follow instructions very well, it needs to be trained with a specific dataset.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@46",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@49",
              "__OiQznq4ao@63",
              "__OiQznq4ao@66",
              "__OiQznq4ao@68",
              "__OiQznq4ao@70"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p01.05",
            "text": "Fine-tuning here means training a pre-trained LLM again so that it becomes better at responding to instructions.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@79",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@81",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@84",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@85",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@148",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@150",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@152",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@156"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p01.06",
            "text": "More specifically, fine-tuning on instruction data means modifying the weights and parameters of the GPT model so that it can learn to understand instruction input-output pairs from a specific dataset.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "__OiQznq4ao@1108",
              "__OiQznq4ao@1111",
              "__OiQznq4ao@1113",
              "__OiQznq4ao@1114",
              "__OiQznq4ao@1117",
              "__OiQznq4ao@1120",
              "__OiQznq4ao@1122"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch06.s01.p02",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p02.01",
            "text": "That raises the next question: what does the instruction-tuning dataset look like?",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p02.02",
            "text": "In instruction fine-tuning, the dataset consists of instructions and the desired responses.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@50",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@52",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@55",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@57",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@59",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@61"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p02.03",
            "text": "Some entries also include an additional input field.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@76",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@79",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@97",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@99",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@103",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@105"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p02.04",
            "text": "The dataset used here contains 1,100 entries of instructions, inputs, and outputs.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "__OiQznq4ao@35",
              "__OiQznq4ao@37",
              "__OiQznq4ao@41",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@246",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@248",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@67",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@69",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@72"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p02.05",
            "text": "These entries come from various fields, including English, geography, and general knowledge.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "__OiQznq4ao@44",
              "__OiQznq4ao@47",
              "__OiQznq4ao@49"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p02.06",
            "text": "The aim of using this dataset is to teach the LLM to correctly follow instructions.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "__OiQznq4ao@49",
              "__OiQznq4ao@51",
              "__OiQznq4ao@53"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p02.07",
            "text": "For example, one entry uses the instruction \"translate the following sentence into French,\" the input \"where is the nearest restaurant,\" and the output as the French translation.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@73",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@74",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@76",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@79",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@81"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p02.08",
            "text": "Another uses the instruction \"rewrite the following sentence so that it is in active voice,\" the input \"the cake was baked by Sarah,\" and the output \"Sarah baked the cake.\"",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@83",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@85",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@88",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@91",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@94"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p02.09",
            "text": "Some pairs have no separate input field, because the sentence or question is included directly in the instruction.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@97",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@99",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@101",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@103",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@105",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@109",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@111",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@114"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ch06.s01.p03",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p03.01",
            "text": "Once the data is collected, it must be divided for training and evaluation.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p03.02",
            "text": "The dataset was split into training, testing, and validation sets using 85% for training, 10% for testing, and 5% for validation.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@225",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@226",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@229",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@232",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@328",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@330",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@332",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@335",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@338",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@117",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@121",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@124",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@127"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p03.03",
            "text": "With 1,100 total pairs, this split gives 935 training examples, 55 validation examples, and 110 test examples.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@340",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@342",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@345",
              "bkUkcyL_Xxc@348"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s01.p03.04",
            "text": "Even though the full dataset has 1,100 instruction-input-output pairs, using 85% for training means the actual training set is only about 800 pairs.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@2797",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@2799",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@2802",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@2805",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@2807"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "invalid_citation_sentences": 0
  }
}
